questions.q:
In the following question, select the related word pair
from the given alternatives :
Tuberculosis : Lungs :: Typhoid : ?

questions.explanation:
According to ‘Scoping Report on Antimicrobial Resistance in
India’ released by the Department of Biotechnology (DBT)
in November 2017, main reasons for the occurrence of multi-
drug resistance (MDR) in microbial pathogens in India are :
(i) High consumption of broad-spectrum antibiotics;
(ii) Injudicious use of antibiotic fixed-dose combinations;
(iii) S elf-medication, access to antibiotics without
prescription and taking incorrect doses of antibiotics
to cure diseases;
(iv) Cultural activities like mass bathing in rivers;
(v) Heavy use of antibiotics in livestock farming;
(vi) Pharmaceutical industry pollution;
(vii) Poor sanitation facilities and disposal of untreated
sewage in water bodies;
(viii) Poor infection prevention practices in healthcare
settings; etc.
Thus reasons given in statements 2 and 3 are correct.
